</div><div class="ltx_page_content">
<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document"> Exploring the Impact of Parameter Update Magnitude on Forgetting and
Generalization of Continual Learning </h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">JinLi He
</span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Liang Bai
</span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Xian Yang
</span><span id="id1" class="ltx_note ltx_note_frontmatter ltx_thanks_correspondence ltx_role_thanks"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_type">thanks: </span>
J. He and L. Bai are with Institute of Intelligent Information Processing, Shanxi University, Taiyuan, 030006, China (Corresponding author: Liang Bai)
<br class="ltx_break">Email: hejinli@sxu.edu.cn, bailiang@sxu.edu.cn
X. Yang is with Alliance Manchester Business School, The University of Manchester, Manchester, M13 9PL, UK. Email: xian.yang@manchester.ac.uk </span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">The magnitude of parameter updates are considered a key factor in continual learning. However, most existing studies focus on designing diverse update strategies, while a theoretical understanding of the underlying mechanisms remains limited. Therefore, we characterize model’s forgetting from the perspective of parameter update magnitude and formalize it as knowledge degradation induced by task-specific drift in the parameter space, which has not been fully captured in previous studies due to their assumption of a unified parameter space. By deriving the optimal parameter update magnitude that minimizes forgetting, we unify two representative update paradigms, frozen training and initialized training, within an optimization framework for constrained parameter updates. Our theoretical results further reveals that sequence tasks with small parameter distances exhibit better generalization and less forgetting under frozen training rather than initialized training. These theoretical insights inspire a novel hybrid parameter update strategy that adaptively adjusts update magnitude based on gradient directions. Experiments on deep neural networks demonstrate that this hybrid approach outperforms standard training strategies, providing new theoretical perspectives and practical inspiration for designing efficient and scalable continual learning algorithms.</p>
  
</div>
<div class="ltx_keywords">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_keywords">Index Terms: </h6>Continual Learning, Learning Theory, Incremental Learning.

</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">I </span><span id="S1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Introduction</span></h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Traditional machine learning typically assume closed-environment settings in which critical factors in the learning process remain constant <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>. However, data often arrive continuously in real-world applications, and collecting and storing all observed data becomes impractical due to escalating storage requirements, increasing computational costs, and potential privacy concerns <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>. A more practical alternative is to incrementally update the model in real time as new data become available <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike traditional approaches that capture static data distributions, continual learning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> aims to learn from data that arrive sequentially with the goal of maintaining reliable performance across all tasks. This paradigm aims to mimic human learning by incrementally acquiring new skills throughout their lifecycle <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>. However, a key challenge is catastrophic forgetting <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>, <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>, where models suffer a significant degradation in performance on previously learned data after adapting to new ones.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In recent years, numerous methods have been proposed to address catastrophic forgetting <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>. One approach <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite> constrains parameters to prevent deviation from the solution space of previous tasks. Another approach <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite> dynamically allocates specific network parameters or modules to each incoming task. Additionally, incorporating previous data <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>, <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> by storing and replaying portions of previous datasets is a simple yet effective strategy. Although numerous methods have contributed to mitigate catastrophic forgetting, some studies suggest that existing algorithms still suffer from computational, memory, and storage inefficiencies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>, <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>, <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>. Some approaches even require more parameter updates than retraining from scratch <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>. Therefore, it is essential to explore effective optimization paths on the parameter update magnitudes for practical applications.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we address fundamental questions driving this research domain: Is catastrophic forgetting solely caused by changes in a subset of parameters? When does freezing most parameters outperform training all parameters? While stability in prior tasks can be maintained through cross-task parameter sharing and additional task-specific parameters enhance plasticity for learning new tasks, does this also exacerbate forgetting? How much parameter updating is sufficient to achieve strong performance on new tasks?</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To address the above questions, a mathematical analysis is required to examine parameter-space separation and forgetting dynamics. However, characterizing parameter separation in sequential tasks is inherently more complex than in static scenarios, and variations in training strategies and optimization objectives further compound this difficulty. The main contributions of this study are summarized as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We characterize forgetting under frozen training and initialized training and derive the optimal update magnitude for minimizing forgetting. The results demonstrate that frozen training outperform initialized training when sequential tasks are close in parameter space.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We propose an adaptive hybrid update framework that dynamically adjusts update magnitude according to the gradient direction in parameter space, enabling a finer and flexible trade-off between stability and plasticity.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Experiments on deep neural networks with real-world datasets indicate that the proposed hybrid update framework consistently outperforms standard training strategies, demonstrating that our theoretical insights guide practical algorithm design in continual learning.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">II </span><span id="S2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Previous Research</span></h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Empirical Research on Continual Learning. Existing continual learning methods can generally be categorized into regularization-based, replay-based, and architecture-based approaches <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>, <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>, <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>. Regularization-based methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>, <a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>, <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>, <a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite> preserve previous knowledge by penalizing changes in parameters or prediction functions, and they typically require storing frozen copies of previous models as references. Weight regularization selectively constrains updates to parameters that are important for earlier tasks, while function regularization restricts intermediate representations or final predictions to mitigate forgetting through knowledge distillation. Replay-based methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>, <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>, <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>, <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite> revisit previous data distributions by storing or generating samples from previous tasks, and can be further divided into sample replay and generative replay. Sample replay stores a limited number of samples from previous tasks in a replay buffer and trains the model jointly with data from the current task. Generative replay, in contrast, introduces an auxiliary generative model to synthesize pseudo-replay data, with the generator itself being incrementally updated over time. Architecture-based methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>, <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>, <a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">48</a>, <a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite> allocate isolated parameters or submodules to each task during training. In recent years, continual learning built upon pre-trained models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>, <a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>, <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite> have enabled training across sequence tasks from a stronger initialization, further mitigating model’s forgetting by leveraging transferable and generalizable features across tasks.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given that catastrophic forgetting primarily stems from parameter updates displacing previously learned knowledge, we analyze the following scenarios. When the model is fully frozen, it preserves performance on previously seen data but at the cost of being unable to acquire new knowledge; conversely, fine-tuning the model with new data allows it to capture current pattern and rapidly adapt to new tasks but often degrades prior experience. These contrasts motivate us to rethink: how can we prevent the loss of previously learned knowledge while training on new tasks, thereby enabling efficient and sustainable intelligent systems? And how many parameter updates are sufficient to learn a specific task while minimizing forgetting and achieving strong performance on incoming tasks?</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Theoretical Research on Continual Learning. Although empirical studies on continual learning have made substantial progress, related theoretical research <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>, <a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>, <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite> remains limited. In this context, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite> extends function regularization beyond weight regularization by modeling Gaussian processes as function priors for learning subsequent tasks. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">57</a>]</cite> studies how teacher–student relationships influence knowledge distillation. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite> connects continual learning with alternating projection and Kaczmarz methods, providing worst-case forgetting analyses. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite> decomposes class-incremental learning into intra-task prediction and task-identity prediction, linking the latter to out-of-distribution detection. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>]</cite> formulates continual learning with pre-trained models as intra-task prediction, task-identity inference, and task-adaptive prediction. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>]</cite> proves the learnability of class-incremental learning from a predictive probability viewpoint. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>]</cite> analyzes forgetting and generalization errors in overparameterized models. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>]</cite> analyzed how the generalization performance of transfer learning evolves as the number of features increases, under both underfitting and overfitting conditions. They found that in scenarios with high noise levels and small true parameters, allocating additional redundant features to specific tasks leads to better generalization performance. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>]</cite> identifies plasticity loss in long-sequence learning and proposes continual backpropagation. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">65</a>]</cite> proposes new evaluation metric to quantify representation forgetting beyond prediction function forgetting.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F1" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="S2.F1.3" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S2.F1.3.1" class="ltx_text"><img src="2602.20796v1/picture/share2.png" id="S2.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/281;" width="476" height="281" alt="Refer to caption"></span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 1</span>: </span><span id="S2.F1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Switching tasks shifts target parameter space, causing forgetting in continual learning. The red symbols shows that a shared space enables fast adaptation and knowledge retention.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">However, existing theoretical research has not provided an explicit analysis of parameter space separation under different update strategies. This work differs in that it unifies two representative update paradigms, frozen training and initialized training, within an optimization framework that constrains parameter updates, and derives the optimal parameter update magnitude that minimizes forgetting, offering a perspective orthogonal to existing theoretical analyses.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">III </span><span id="S3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Problem Setup</span></h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In a continual learning scenario with <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> sequential tasks, the dataset for task <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted by <math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{k}=\{(R_{(k)}^{i},y_{(k)}^{i})\}_{i=1}^{N_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{k}=\{(R_{(k)}^{i},y_{(k)}^{i})\}_{i=1}^{N_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>, consisting of <math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> input-label pairs, where <math id="S3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> indexes the task identity. Starting from an initial parameter vector <math id="S3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>, the model is trained sequentially, yielding parameter estimates <math id="S3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{(1)},\theta_{(2)},\ldots,\theta_{(M)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{(1)},\theta_{(2)},\ldots,\theta_{(M)}</annotation></semantics></math>. With analytical tractability, the Gaussian features and noise are adapted. The objective is to learn an optimal parameter update model under fixed model capacity that consistently satisfies: (1) a finite parameter overhead as the number of tasks increases, and (2) optimal magnitude of parameter updates across training stages.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To achieve the above objectives, the parameter space is split into shared and task-specific parts, with task-specific parts quantified to minimize catastrophic forgetting. The optimized model is denoted as <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{(k)}=X_{(k)}^{\top}u_{(k)}+Z_{(k)}^{\top}q_{(k)}+\varepsilon_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{(k)}=X_{(k)}^{\top}u_{(k)}+Z_{(k)}^{\top}q_{(k)}+\varepsilon_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{(k)}\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times n_{(k)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{(k)}\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times n_{(k)}}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the features associated with the shared parameters <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{(k)}\in\mathbb{R}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{(k)}\in\mathbb{R}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{(k)}\in\mathbb{R}^{p_{(k)}\times n_{(k)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{(k)}\in\mathbb{R}^{p_{(k)}\times n_{(k)}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes features associated with the task-specific parameters <math id="S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{(k)}\in\mathbb{R}^{p_{(k)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{(k)}\in\mathbb{R}^{p_{(k)}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Performance on task <math id="S3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is measured by squared loss, following the metric from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">66</a>, <a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>, <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Note: For clarity, we describe the notation commonly used in this paper. Matrices are denoted by uppercase letters <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, and vectors by lowercase letters <math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>. For vectors <math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, their inner product is <math id="S3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{u},\mathbf{q}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐪</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{u},\mathbf{q}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. For matrices <math id="S3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, their inner product is denoted by <math id="S3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Z}\rangle_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Z}\rangle_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{a}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{a}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="S3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm of vector <math id="S3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{a}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{V}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{V}\|</annotation></semantics></math> denote the spectral norm of matrix <math id="S3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐕</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Frozen Training vs Initialized Training</span></h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we first introduce initialized training and frozen training, two widely used training modes in continual learning. We then characterize the theoretical error and compare their performance analytically from a unified theoretical perspective. Next, we derive the optimal update conditions that minimize forgetting under a fixed model capacity. Finally, we demonstrate that frozen training outperforms initialization training when the parameter spaces are close in distance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.20796v1/picture/train2.png" id="S4.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/310;" width="476" height="310" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 2</span>: </span><span id="S4.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Frozen training and initialized training. Initialized training updates all parameters during training, whereas frozen training preserves general knowledge by fixing most parameters and adapts to new tasks using a few trainable parameters.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{u}_{(k-1)},\tilde{q}_{(k-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{u}_{(k-1)},\tilde{q}_{(k-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the parameters after training the <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k-1</annotation></semantics></math>-th task. When training the <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th task, a widely used approach is initialization training, in which all parameters are reoptimized starting from the previously learned model. An alternative strategy, referred to as frozen training, freezes a subset of parameters and allocates only a small number of parameters for learning new tasks. The update processes for these two training modes are formalized as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training Rule A ( Frozen Training ).</span> The knowledge acquisition is achieved by freezing the parameters <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{u}_{(k-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{u}_{(k-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and setting them as <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{u}_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{u}_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>, while training only <math id="S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>, a small set of parameters. The update process is as follows.</p>
<table id="S4.E1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E1X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E1X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\arg\min_{q}||\widetilde{q}_{(k)}-\widetilde{q}_{(k-1)}||^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>q</mi></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\arg\min_{q}||\widetilde{q}_{(k)}-\widetilde{q}_{(k-1)}||^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E1Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E1Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{s.t.}\;Z_{(k)}^{T}q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{s.t.}\;Z_{(k)}^{T}q</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E1Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=y_{(k)}-X_{(k)}^{\top}\tilde{u}_{(k-1)}-Z_{(k)}^{\top}\tilde{q}_{(k-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=y_{(k)}-X_{(k)}^{\top}\tilde{u}_{(k-1)}-Z_{(k)}^{\top}\tilde{q}_{(k-1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=\widetilde{q}_{(k)}-\widetilde{q}_{(k-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=\widetilde{q}_{(k)}-\widetilde{q}_{(k-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u_{(k)}-u_{(j)}\|=\delta,k\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u_{(k)}-u_{(j)}\|=\delta,k\neq j</annotation></semantics></math> as the parameter discrepancy over the shared subspace. Empirical analysis <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>]</cite> indicates that in continual learning, only a small subset of parameters is task-specific and sensitive to task changes, while most capture shared knowledge across tasks. Under frozen training, the model retains the parameters <math id="S4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{u}{(k-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{u}{(k-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> to enable knowledge retention, and adapts to new tasks by learning the <math id="S4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark IV.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <a href="#S4.E1" title="In IV Frozen Training vs Initialized Training ‣ Exploring the Impact of Parameter Update Magnitude on Forgetting and Generalization of Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#S4.E2" title="In IV Frozen Training vs Initialized Training ‣ Exploring the Impact of Parameter Update Magnitude on Forgetting and Generalization of Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> presents the expression for the case where <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{(k)}&gt;n_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{(k)}&gt;n_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>. The complementary case <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{(k)}&gt;p_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{(k)}&gt;p_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>, along with the corresponding error analysis, is deferred to Appendix A.1.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training Rule B ( Initialized Training ) .</span> The learned parameters <math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{u}_{(k-1)},\tilde{q}_{(k-1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{u}_{(k-1)},\tilde{q}_{(k-1)})</annotation></semantics></math> serve as initialization for current task, and the <math id="S4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{u}_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{u}_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> are then joined optimized to iteratively update the learner. The update process is as follows.</p>
<table id="S4.E2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E2X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E2X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname*{arg\,min}_{\tilde{u}_{(k)},\,\tilde{q}_{(k)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname*{arg\,min}_{\tilde{u}_{(k)},\,\tilde{q}_{(k)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E2X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\tilde{u}_{(k)}-\tilde{u}_{(k-1)}\|^{2}+\|\tilde{q}_{(k)}-\tilde{q}_{(k-1)}\|^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\tilde{u}_{(k)}-\tilde{u}_{(k-1)}\|^{2}+\|\tilde{q}_{(k)}-\tilde{q}_{(k-1)}\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E2Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E2Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{s.t. }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext>s.t.</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{s.t. }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E2Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{(k)}^{\top}\tilde{u}_{(k)}+Z_{(k)}^{\top}\tilde{q}_{(k)}=y_{(k)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{(k)}^{\top}\tilde{u}_{(k)}+Z_{(k)}^{\top}\tilde{q}_{(k)}=y_{(k)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{u}_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{u}_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> are jointly optimized to achieve full fine-tuning of parameters. The following lemma provides the average difference between parameters trained and their prior true parameters under frozen training.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma IV.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under frozen training, define <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=1-\frac{n_{(1)}}{p+p_{(1)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=1-\frac{n_{(1)}}{p+p_{(1)}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{A}=1-\frac{n_{(2)}}{p_{(2)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{A}=1-\frac{n_{(2)}}{p_{(2)}}</annotation></semantics></math>. After completing <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{u}_{(2)},\tilde{q}_{(2)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{u}_{(2)},\tilde{q}_{(2)})</annotation></semantics></math>, the average deviation from the previous task’s parameters is given by:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E3X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E3X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}\!\left[\|\tilde{u}_{(2)}-u_{(1)}\|^{2}+\|\tilde{q}_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|^{2}\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}\!\left[\|\tilde{u}_{(2)}-u_{(1)}\|^{2}+\|\tilde{q}_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|^{2}\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E3Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E3Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r[\lVert u_{(1)}\rVert^{2}+r_{A}\lVert q_{(1)}\rVert^{2}+\frac{n_{(2)}\lVert u_{(2)}\rVert^{2}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r[\lVert u_{(1)}\rVert^{2}+r_{A}\lVert q_{(1)}\rVert^{2}+\frac{n_{(2)}\lVert u_{(2)}\rVert^{2}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E3Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E3Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+(1-r_{A})\lVert q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\rVert^{2}+\frac{n_{(2)}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(1-r_{A})\lVert q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\rVert^{2}+\frac{n_{(2)}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E3Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E3Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{n_{(1)}v_{(1)}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{p+p_{(1)}-n_{(1)}-1}+\frac{n_{(2)}(1-r)\delta^{2}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{n_{(1)}v_{(1)}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{p+p_{(1)}-n_{(1)}-1}+\frac{n_{(2)}(1-r)\delta^{2}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{(1)}=1+\frac{p\,n_{(2)}}{(p+p_{(1)})(p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1)}-\frac{p_{(1)}n_{(2)}}{(p+p_{(1)})p_{(2)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{(1)}=1+\frac{p\,n_{(2)}}{(p+p_{(1)})(p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1)}-\frac{p_{(1)}n_{(2)}}{(p+p_{(1)})p_{(2)}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Appendix A.1 provides the proof of Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma IV.2. ‣ IV Frozen Training vs Initialized Training ‣ Exploring the Impact of Parameter Update Magnitude on Forgetting and Generalization of Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV.2</span></a>, discusses the case where <math id="S4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{(2)}&lt;n_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{(2)}&lt;n_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and presents the counterpart results for initialized training. Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma IV.2. ‣ IV Frozen Training vs Initialized Training ‣ Exploring the Impact of Parameter Update Magnitude on Forgetting and Generalization of Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV.2</span></a> shows that the average magnitude relative to the original parameters depends on task discrepancy <math id="S4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\rVert^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the noise levels <math id="S4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the parameter-sample ratio <math id="S4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. The following lemma presents the average forgetting under the frozen training.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma IV.3</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under frozen training, the expected forgetting <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{FRO}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{FRO}]</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{(2)}&gt;n_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{(2)}&gt;n_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the previous task after parameter updates is given by:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E4X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{FRO}]=\frac{n_{(2)}(1-r)\delta^{2}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{FRO}]=\frac{n_{(2)}(1-r)\delta^{2}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E4Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+r\Bigl[(r_{A}-1)\|q_{(1)}\|^{2}+\frac{n_{(2)}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1}\|u_{(2)}\|^{2}\Bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+r\Bigl[(r_{A}-1)\|q_{(1)}\|^{2}+\frac{n_{(2)}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1}\|u_{(2)}\|^{2}\Bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E4Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+(1-r_{A})\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|^{2}+(\frac{pn_{(2)}}{(p+p_{(1)})(p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(1-r_{A})\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|^{2}+(\frac{pn_{(2)}}{(p+p_{(1)})(p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E4Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{p_{(1)}n_{(2)}}{(p+p_{(1)})p_{(2)}})\frac{n_{(1)}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{p+p_{(1)}-n_{(1)}-1}+\frac{n_{(2)}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{p_{(1)}n_{(2)}}{(p+p_{(1)})p_{(2)}})\frac{n_{(1)}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{p+p_{(1)}-n_{(1)}-1}+\frac{n_{(2)}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is provided in Appendix A.2. Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma IV.3. ‣ IV Frozen Training vs Initialized Training ‣ Exploring the Impact of Parameter Update Magnitude on Forgetting and Generalization of Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV.3</span></a> shows that with <math id="S4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p+p_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p+p_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> fixed, increasing <math id="S4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> weakens general knowledge acquisition, whereas decreasing <math id="S4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> results in insufficient training. These two effects impose mutual constraints on the average forgetting rate, and the following theorem characterizes the minimal update condition.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem IV.4</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With fixed capacity <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p+p_{(2)}=K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p+p_{(2)}=K</annotation></semantics></math>, an extremum arises with trainable <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> under frozen training, provided the following condition regarding <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> holds.</span></p>
<table id="S4.E5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E5X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E5X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\xi-\eta)p_{(2)}^{2}+(n_{(2)}+1)^{2}\xi=2(n_{(2)}+1)p_{(2)}\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\xi-\eta)p_{(2)}^{2}+(n_{(2)}+1)^{2}\xi=2(n_{(2)}+1)p_{(2)}\xi</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">And the parameter <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E6X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{(2)}=\frac{(n_{(2)}+1)(\xi+\sqrt{\xi\eta})}{\xi-\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{(2)}=\frac{(n_{(2)}+1)(\xi+\sqrt{\xi\eta})}{\xi-\eta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Where <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi&gt;\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi&gt;\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K-n_{(1)}-1&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K-n_{(1)}-1&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and their expressions are given by the following formulas</span></p>
<table id="S4.E7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E7X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E7X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\xi=r\|q_{(1)}\|^{2}-\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\xi=r\|q_{(1)}\|^{2}-\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E7Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E7Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta=r||u_{(2)}||^{2}+(1-r)\delta^{2}+\sigma_{(2)}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta=r||u_{(2)}||^{2}+(1-r)\delta^{2}+\sigma_{(2)}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E7Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E7Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{n_{(1)}p\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{(K-n_{(1)}-1)K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{n_{(1)}p\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{(K-n_{(1)}-1)K}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span> According to <math id="S4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{FRO}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{FRO}]</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S4.E4" title="In Lemma IV.3. ‣ IV Frozen Training vs Initialized Training ‣ Exploring the Impact of Parameter Update Magnitude on Forgetting and Generalization of Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, taking the derivative with respect to <math id="S4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> yielding</p>
<table id="S4.E8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E8X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E8X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial[\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}]}{\partial p_{(2)}}=\frac{n_{(2)}r\|q_{(1)}\|^{2}}{p_{(2)}^{2}}-\frac{n_{(2)}r\|u_{(2)}\|^{2}}{(p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial[\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}]}{\partial p_{(2)}}=\frac{n_{(2)}r\|q_{(1)}\|^{2}}{p_{(2)}^{2}}-\frac{n_{(2)}r\|u_{(2)}\|^{2}}{(p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E8Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E8Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{n_{(2)}(1-r)\delta^{2}}{(p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1)^{2}}-\frac{n_{(2)}\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|^{2}}{p_{(2)}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{n_{(2)}(1-r)\delta^{2}}{(p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1)^{2}}-\frac{n_{(2)}\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|^{2}}{p_{(2)}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E8Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E8Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{pn_{(2)}}{K(p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1)^{2}}\cdot\frac{n_{(1)}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{(K-n_{(1)}-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{pn_{(2)}}{K(p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1)^{2}}\cdot\frac{n_{(1)}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{(K-n_{(1)}-1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E8Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E8Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{n_{(2)}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{(p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{n_{(2)}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{(p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p8.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{(2)}=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{(2)}=x</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, this derivative becomes a function of <math id="S4.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>. The points where this expression equals zero can be calculated to obtain the corresponding equation</p>
<table id="S4.E9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E9X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E9X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left[r\|q_{(1)}\|^{2}-\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|^{2}\right]\cdot(x-n_{(2)}-1)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[r\|q_{(1)}\|^{2}-\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|^{2}\right]\cdot(x-n_{(2)}-1)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E9Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E9Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E9Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x^{2}\cdot[r\|u_{(2)}\|^{2}+(1-r)\delta^{2}+v_{(2)}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}+\sigma_{(2)}^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x^{2}\cdot[r\|u_{(2)}\|^{2}+(1-r)\delta^{2}+v_{(2)}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}+\sigma_{(2)}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p8.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{(2)}=\frac{p}{p+p_{(1)}}\cdot\frac{n_{(1)}}{p+p_{(1)}-n_{(1)}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{(2)}=\frac{p}{p+p_{(1)}}\cdot\frac{n_{(1)}}{p+p_{(1)}-n_{(1)}-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Solving the above equation yields the solution satisfy the condition as follows</p>
<table id="S4.E10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E10X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E10X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x=\frac{(n_{(2)}+1)(\xi+\sqrt{\xi\eta})}{\xi-\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x=\frac{(n_{(2)}+1)(\xi+\sqrt{\xi\eta})}{\xi-\eta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p8.4" class="ltx_p">The complete version are provided in Appendix A.3. Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem IV.4. ‣ IV Frozen Training vs Initialized Training ‣ Exploring the Impact of Parameter Update Magnitude on Forgetting and Generalization of Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV.4</span></a> shows that the average forgetting with respect to the trainable parameter <math id="S4.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> reaches an extremum when <math id="S4.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi&gt;\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi&gt;\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, beyond which further increases in <math id="S4.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> yield diminishing returns. In particular, a plateau occurs when <math id="S4.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|</annotation></semantics></math> is small. The following lemma describes average forgetting under initialized training.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma IV.5</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under initialized training, define <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{B}=1-\frac{n_{(2)}}{p+p_{(2)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{B}=1-\frac{n_{(2)}}{p+p_{(2)}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The expected forgetting <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{TUN}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{TUN}]</annotation></semantics></math> relative to the previous task is expressed as follows.</span></p>
<table id="S4.E11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E11X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E11X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{TUN}]=r[(r_{B}-1)(\|u_{(1)}\|^{2}+\|q_{(1)}\|^{2})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{TUN}]=r[(r_{B}-1)(\|u_{(1)}\|^{2}+\|q_{(1)}\|^{2})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E11Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E11Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+(1-r_{B})\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|^{2}+(1-r_{B})\delta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(1-r_{B})\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|^{2}+(1-r_{B})\delta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E11Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E11Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{n_{(1)}(r_{B}-1)\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{p+p_{(1)}-n_{(1)}-1}+\frac{n_{(2)}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{p+p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{n_{(1)}(r_{B}-1)\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{p+p_{(1)}-n_{(1)}-1}+\frac{n_{(2)}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{p+p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is provided in Appendix A.4. From the above formula, <math id="S4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{TUN}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{TUN}]</annotation></semantics></math> depends on <math id="S4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|q_{(1)}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|q_{(1)}\|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u_{(1)}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u_{(1)}\|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas <math id="S4.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{FRO}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{FRO}]</annotation></semantics></math> depends on <math id="S4.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|q_{(1)}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|q_{(1)}\|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u_{(2)}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u_{(2)}\|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|</annotation></semantics></math>. Compared to <a href="#S4.E4" title="In Lemma IV.3. ‣ IV Frozen Training vs Initialized Training ‣ Exploring the Impact of Parameter Update Magnitude on Forgetting and Generalization of Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, initialized training introducing trainable parameter reduces the term involving <math id="S4.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> but also introduces term <math id="S4.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(r_{B}-1)\|u_{(1)}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(r_{B}-1)\|u_{(1)}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The following theorem compares forgetting under frozen training and initialized training.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem IV.6</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For frozen training and initialized training, the expected forgetting for any <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{(2)}&gt;n_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{(2)}&gt;n_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{FRO}]&lt;\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{TUN}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{FRO}]&lt;\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{TUN}]</annotation></semantics></math> under</span></p>
<table id="S4.E12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E12X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E12X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma_{1}\|u_{(1)}\|^{2}+\gamma_{2}\|u_{(2)}\|^{2}+r\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma_{1}\|u_{(1)}\|^{2}+\gamma_{2}\|u_{(2)}\|^{2}+r\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E12Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E12Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\gamma_{3}\delta^{2}+\gamma_{4}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}+\gamma_{5}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}&lt;\|q_{(1)}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\gamma_{3}\delta^{2}+\gamma_{4}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}+\gamma_{5}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}&lt;\|q_{(1)}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Where the formulaic expressions for <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2},\gamma_{3},\gamma_{4}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2},\gamma_{3},\gamma_{4},</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{5}</annotation></semantics></math>, together with the corresponding expressions for the constants <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{(3)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{(3)}</annotation></semantics></math> through <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{(6)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{(6)}</annotation></semantics></math>, are provided as follows</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma_{1}=\frac{1-r_{B}}{r_{B}-r_{A}};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma_{1}=\frac{1-r_{B}}{r_{B}-r_{A}};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma_{2}=\frac{n_{(2)}}{(r_{B}-r_{A})v_{(4)}};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma_{2}=\frac{n_{(2)}}{(r_{B}-r_{A})v_{(4)}};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma_{3}=\frac{(1-r)n_{(2)}-(1-r_{B})v_{(4)}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})v_{(4)}};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma_{3}=\frac{(1-r)n_{(2)}-(1-r_{B})v_{(4)}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})v_{(4)}};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma_{4}=\frac{n_{(1)}\left[pn_{(2)}-(1-r_{A})p_{(1)}v_{(4)}\right]}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}v_{(5)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma_{4}=\frac{n_{(1)}\left[pn_{(2)}-(1-r_{A})p_{(1)}v_{(4)}\right]}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}v_{(5)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{\left[(1-r_{B})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}\right]n_{(1)}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}v_{(5)}};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{\left[(1-r_{B})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}\right]n_{(1)}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}v_{(5)}};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma_{5}=\frac{pn_{(2)}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1)v_{(4)}};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma_{5}=\frac{pn_{(2)}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1)v_{(4)}};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{(3)}=1+\frac{2n_{(2)}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{(3)}=1+\frac{2n_{(2)}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{(4)}=p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{(4)}=p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{(5)}=p+p_{(1)}-n_{(1)}-1;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{(5)}=p+p_{(1)}-n_{(1)}-1;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{(6)}=p_{(2)}+n_{(2)}-1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{(6)}=p_{(2)}+n_{(2)}-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span>
Comparing the average forgetting under under the two training modes, and examining the differences across the various terms, the following inequality is obtained</p>
<table id="S4.E22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E22X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E22X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r(r_{B}-1)&lt;0;\quad r_{B}&gt;r_{A};\quad\frac{n_{(2)}r}{v_{(4)}}&gt;0;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">;</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r(r_{B}-1)&lt;0;\quad r_{B}&gt;r_{A};\quad\frac{n_{(2)}r}{v_{(4)}}&gt;0;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E22Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E22Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{n_{(2)}(1-r)}{v_{(4)}}&lt;(1-r_{B});\quad\frac{n_{(2)}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{p+v_{(4)}}&lt;\frac{n_{(2)}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{v_{(4)}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&lt;</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="1.167em">;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{n_{(2)}(1-r)}{v_{(4)}}&lt;(1-r_{B});\quad\frac{n_{(2)}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{p+v_{(4)}}&lt;\frac{n_{(2)}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{v_{(4)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p10.2" class="ltx_p">Then, it follows that <math id="S4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{FRO}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{FRO}]</annotation></semantics></math> is smaller than <math id="S4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{TUN}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Forgetting_{TUN}]</annotation></semantics></math> when the following inequality holds</p>
<table id="S4.E23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E23X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E23X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{(1-r_{B})\|u_{(1)}\|^{2}}{r_{B}-r_{A}}+\frac{n_{(2)}\|u_{(2)}\|^{2}}{(r_{B}-r_{A})v_{(4)}}+r\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{(1-r_{B})\|u_{(1)}\|^{2}}{r_{B}-r_{A}}+\frac{n_{(2)}\|u_{(2)}\|^{2}}{(r_{B}-r_{A})v_{(4)}}+r\|q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E23Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E23Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{[(1-r)n_{(2)}-(1-r_{B})v_{(4)}]\delta^{2}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})v_{(4)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{[(1-r)n_{(2)}-(1-r_{B})v_{(4)}]\delta^{2}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})v_{(4)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E23Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E23Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{\left[pn_{(2)}-p_{(1)}(1-r_{A})v_{(4)}\right]n_{(1)}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}v_{(5)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{\left[pn_{(2)}-p_{(1)}(1-r_{A})v_{(4)}\right]n_{(1)}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}v_{(5)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E23Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E23Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{\left[(1-r_{B})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}\right]n_{(1)}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}v_{(5)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{\left[(1-r_{B})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}\right]n_{(1)}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}v_{(5)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E23Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E23Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{pn_{(2)}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+v_{(4)})v_{(4)}}&lt;||q_{(1)}||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{pn_{(2)}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+v_{(4)})v_{(4)}}&lt;||q_{(1)}||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem IV.6. ‣ IV Frozen Training vs Initialized Training ‣ Exploring the Impact of Parameter Update Magnitude on Forgetting and Generalization of Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV.6</span></a> demonstrates that when <a href="#S4.E12" title="In Theorem IV.6. ‣ IV Frozen Training vs Initialized Training ‣ Exploring the Impact of Parameter Update Magnitude on Forgetting and Generalization of Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> holds, the frozen training outperforms initialized training in reducing forgetting, which requires compact parameter space. The following proposition further characterizes average generalization under frozen training beyond the forgetting.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition IV.7</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under frozen training, for any <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{(2)}&gt;n_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{(2)}&gt;n_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>, the average generalization <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Generalization_{FRO}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Generalization_{FRO}]</annotation></semantics></math> across learned tasks can be expressed as follows below.</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Generalization_{FRO}]=\frac{1-rr_{A}}{2}\lVert q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\rVert^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Generalization_{FRO}]=\frac{1-rr_{A}}{2}\lVert q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{r}{2}\Bigl[\lVert u_{(1)}\rVert^{2}+v_{(3)}\lVert u_{(2)}\rVert^{2}+r_{A}\lVert q_{(1)}\rVert^{2}+r_{A}\lVert q_{(2)}\rVert^{2}\Bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{r}{2}\Bigl[\lVert u_{(1)}\rVert^{2}+v_{(3)}\lVert u_{(2)}\rVert^{2}+r_{A}\lVert q_{(1)}\rVert^{2}+r_{A}\lVert q_{(2)}\rVert^{2}\Bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{(1-r)v_{(3)}\delta^{2}}{2}+\frac{n_{(1)}v_{(1)}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{p+p_{(1)}-n_{(1)}-1}+\frac{n_{(2)}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{(1-r)v_{(3)}\delta^{2}}{2}+\frac{n_{(1)}v_{(1)}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{p+p_{(1)}-n_{(1)}-1}+\frac{n_{(2)}\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p12.1" class="ltx_p">The detailed proof is provided in Appendix A.6. The Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem7" title="Proposition IV.7. ‣ IV Frozen Training vs Initialized Training ‣ Exploring the Impact of Parameter Update Magnitude on Forgetting and Generalization of Continual Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV.7</span></a> shows that the coefficients of <math id="S4.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert u_{(1)}\rVert^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert u_{(1)}\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert u_{(2)}\rVert^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert u_{(2)}\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert q_{(1)}\rVert^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert q_{(1)}\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert q_{(2)}\rVert^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert q_{(2)}\rVert^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct, indicating that parameter components play varying roles under frozen training. The following corollary compares frozen training and initialized training under average generalization.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark IV.8</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The average generalization under initialized training, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Generalization_{TUN}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Generalization_{TUN}]</annotation></semantics></math>, along with the complete results for <math id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{(2)}&lt;n_{(2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{(2)}&lt;n_{(2)}</annotation></semantics></math>, are detailed in Appendix A.6.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary IV.9</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For frozen training and initialized training, the expected generalization results satisfies satisfies the inequality <math id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Generalization_{FRO}]&lt;\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Generalization_{TUN}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Generalization_{FRO}]&lt;\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Generalization_{TUN}]</annotation></semantics></math> under the following conditions</span></p>
<table id="S4.E25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E25X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\beta_{1}\cdot||u_{(1)}||^{2}+\beta_{2}\cdot||u_{(2)}||^{2}+||q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}||^{2}}{||q_{(1)}||^{2}+||q_{(2)}||^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\beta_{1}\cdot||u_{(1)}||^{2}+\beta_{2}\cdot||u_{(2)}||^{2}+||q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}||^{2}}{||q_{(1)}||^{2}+||q_{(2)}||^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E25Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{\beta_{3}\cdot\delta^{2}+\beta_{4}\cdot\sigma_{(1)}^{2}+\beta_{5}\cdot\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{||q_{(1)}||^{2}+||q_{(2)}||^{2}}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{\beta_{3}\cdot\delta^{2}+\beta_{4}\cdot\sigma_{(1)}^{2}+\beta_{5}\cdot\sigma_{(2)}^{2}}{||q_{(1)}||^{2}+||q_{(2)}||^{2}}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\beta_{2},\beta_{3},\beta_{4},\beta_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\beta_{2},\beta_{3},\beta_{4},\beta_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> are defined as follows:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{1}=\frac{1-r_{B}}{r_{B}-r_{A}};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{1}=\frac{1-r_{B}}{r_{B}-r_{A}};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{2}=\frac{p_{(2)}+n_{(2)}-1-v_{(4)}r_{B}}{\left(r_{B}-r_{A}\right)v_{(4)}};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{2}=\frac{p_{(2)}+n_{(2)}-1-v_{(4)}r_{B}}{\left(r_{B}-r_{A}\right)v_{(4)}};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{3}=\frac{(1-r)v_{(6)}-(1-rr_{B})v_{(6)}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})v_{(4)}};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{3}=\frac{(1-r)v_{(6)}-(1-rr_{B})v_{(6)}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})v_{(4)}};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{4}=\frac{2\left[pn_{(2)}-(1-r_{A})p_{(1)}v_{(4)}\right]n_{(1)}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}v_{(5)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{4}=\frac{2\left[pn_{(2)}-(1-r_{A})p_{(1)}v_{(4)}\right]n_{(1)}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}v_{(5)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{2\left[(1-r_{B})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}\right]n_{(1)}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}v_{(5)}};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{2\left[(1-r_{B})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}\right]n_{(1)}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}v_{(5)}};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta_{5}=\frac{2pn_{(2)}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1)v_{(4)}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta_{5}=\frac{2pn_{(2)}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1)v_{(4)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span>
Comparing the expected generalization across the various coefficients yields the following inequality.</p>
<table id="S4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r\cdot r_{B}&lt;r;\quad r_{B}&lt;(1+\frac{2n_{(2)}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1});" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r\cdot r_{B}&lt;r;\quad r_{B}&lt;(1+\frac{2n_{(2)}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1});</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1-r)(1+\frac{2n_{(2)}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1})&gt;(1-r\cdot r_{B});" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1-r)(1+\frac{2n_{(2)}}{p_{(2)}-n_{(2)}-1})&gt;(1-r\cdot r_{B});</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1+\frac{pn_{(2)}}{(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}}-\frac{p_{(1)}n_{(2)}}{(p+p_{(1)})p_{(2)}})&gt;r_{B}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1+\frac{pn_{(2)}}{(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}}-\frac{p_{(1)}n_{(2)}}{(p+p_{(1)})p_{(2)}})&gt;r_{B}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p13.2" class="ltx_p">Then, it follows that <math id="S4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Generalization_{FRO}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Generalization_{FRO}]</annotation></semantics></math> is smaller than <math id="S4.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Generalization_{TUN}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{u},\tilde{q}}[Generalization_{TUN}]</annotation></semantics></math> provided that</p>
<table id="S4.E34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E34X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E34X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{(1-r_{B})\left\|u_{(1)}\right\|^{2}}{(r_{B}-r_{A})}+\frac{(v_{(6)}-v_{(4)}r_{B})\left\|u_{(2)}\right\|^{2}}{\left(r_{B}-r_{A}\right)v_{(4)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{(1-r_{B})\left\|u_{(1)}\right\|^{2}}{(r_{B}-r_{A})}+\frac{(v_{(6)}-v_{(4)}r_{B})\left\|u_{(2)}\right\|^{2}}{\left(r_{B}-r_{A}\right)v_{(4)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="6" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E34Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E34Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+||q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}||^{2}+\frac{r(r_{B}-1))v_{(6)}\delta^{2}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})v_{(4)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+||q_{(2)}-q_{(1)}||^{2}+\frac{r(r_{B}-1))v_{(6)}\delta^{2}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})v_{(4)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E34Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E34Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{2\left[pn_{(2)}-(1-r_{A})p_{(1)}v_{(4)}\right]n_{(1)}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}v_{(5)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{2\left[pn_{(2)}-(1-r_{A})p_{(1)}v_{(4)}\right]n_{(1)}\sigma_{(1)}^{2}}{r(r_{B}-r_{A})(p+p_{(1)})v_{(4)}v_{(5)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E34Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
